CAT = "sgvlRoadSafety"; SEG = "SAF"
# Paper A: on-the-road safety practices for taxi and private hire drivers.
Q = [
("You have driven for many hours and your eyes keep closing at traffic lights. What should you do?",
 "Stop work and rest", ["Open the windows wide and carry on driving", "Drink a strong coffee and take one more job", "Turn up the radio and drive more slowly"],
 "Fatigue slows your reactions as much as alcohol. Fresh air, coffee or music only mask it for minutes; the only fix is to stop and rest."),
("A passenger in the back seat has not buckled up. What should you do before moving off?",
 "Politely ask them to wear the belt", ["Drive off, as it is their choice", "Wait until you reach the expressway", "Remind them only if police are near"],
 "Everyone in the car must wear a seat belt where one is fitted. A short, polite reminder before moving off protects the passenger and you."),
("You stop at the kerb to let a passenger out on the right side of the car. What is the main danger?",
 "A rider passing on that side", ["The meter running on a little longer than usual", "The passenger forgetting to take a receipt", "A pedestrian walking on the left footway"],
 "A door opened into traffic can hit a cyclist, PMD user or motorcyclist. Ask passengers to get out on the kerb side and check before any door opens."),
("Before a passenger opens a door, what is the safest habit for you as the driver?",
 "Check mirrors and blind spot first", ["Unlock all doors as you brake", "Tell them to open the door quickly", "Switch on the interior light only"],
 "Checking the mirrors and over your shoulder before doors open catches cyclists and riders coming up alongside. Keep the doors locked until it is clear."),
("A booking app pings with a new job while you are driving. What should you do?",
 "Ignore it until you can stop safely", ["Accept it quickly at the next junction", "Hold the phone low and tap accept", "Ask the passenger to accept it for you"],
 "Handling a phone while the car moves is an offence and a common cause of crashes. Set the app up before you move and deal with jobs only when parked safely."),
("Where should a phone used for navigation be placed while you drive?",
 "In a fixed holder", ["On your lap, within easy reach of your hand", "On the passenger seat beside you", "In your hand, held below the windscreen"],
 "A mounted phone set up before the trip lets you glance at directions without holding it. Programme the route while stationary."),
("It starts raining heavily on the PIE. How should you change your driving?",
 "Slow down and double the gap ahead", ["Keep the speed but brake earlier", "Switch on the hazard lights and carry on", "Move into the right lane to overtake"],
 "Wet roads lengthen stopping distances and cut visibility. Drop your speed, leave a much bigger gap and use headlights, not hazard lights, while moving."),
("When are hazard warning lights correctly used?",
 "When stopped as an obstruction", ["When driving slowly through heavy rain", "When parking briefly on a double yellow line", "When thanking a driver who gave way"],
 "Hazard lights warn others that your stationary vehicle is an obstruction, such as after a breakdown. They are not a licence to stop where stopping is not allowed."),
("A passenger says they are late and asks you to speed. What should you do?",
 "Keep to the limit and explain why", ["Speed up on quiet stretches only", "Take a bus lane to save time", "Jump the amber lights to help them"],
 "Your licence, your passenger's safety and other road users come first. Keep to the speed limit and tell the passenger calmly that you will get them there safely."),
("You are approaching a signalised crossing as the light turns amber and you could stop safely. What should you do?",
 "Stop at the stop line", ["Speed up to clear the junction", "Sound the horn and continue", "Slow down and creep through"],
 "Amber means stop unless you are so close that stopping would be unsafe. Rushing an amber light is how red-light crashes happen."),
("You pass a 'Start of silver zone' sign with a speed limit sign attached. What does it tell you?",
 "Watch for elderly pedestrians; keep to the limit", ["A hospital entrance is on the left side", "Cyclists may use the whole lane ahead", "Only taxis may stop for older passengers"],
 "Silver Zones are in estates with many seniors. Slow down, look out for elderly pedestrians crossing and do not exceed the posted speed limit."),
("Children are near a school during dismissal time. How should you drive past?",
 "Slowly, ready to stop for a child", ["At the normal limit, using the horn", "In the right lane to keep away", "Quickly, to clear the area"],
 "Children can dart out from between parked cars. In a school zone keep to the lower limit, cover the brake and watch the kerbs."),
("A cyclist is riding ahead of you in your lane on a narrow road. How should you pass?",
 "Wait, then pass with a wide gap", ["Sound the horn so they move aside", "Squeeze past close to the kerb", "Follow closely until they turn off"],
 "Give a cyclist plenty of space and pass only when it is safe to do so. A horn can startle a rider into a fall."),
("When is your blind spot most likely to hide a motorcyclist?",
 "When you change lanes", ["When you stop at a red light", "When you reverse into a driveway", "When you drive straight ahead slowly"],
 "Motorcycles fit easily into the area your mirrors do not show. A shoulder check before every lane change finds them."),
("After a long day, how can you best plan your shifts to avoid fatigue?",
 "Take regular breaks and enough sleep", ["Drive until the evening peak is over", "Finish every shift with a night job", "Rely on energy drinks between jobs"],
 "Planned breaks and proper sleep are what prevent fatigue. Stimulants wear off suddenly and leave you more tired."),
("You have taken medicine that says it may cause drowsiness. What should you do?",
 "Not drive until it wears off", ["Drive, but use only the expressways", "Drive, but keep the windows open for air", "Take passengers on short trips only"],
 "Drowsy medicine affects judgement and reaction time just as fatigue does. Check the label and ask your doctor or pharmacist before you work."),
("A passenger wants you to stop right at a busy junction to get out. What should you do?",
 "Stop further on, where it is safe", ["Stop at once to avoid an argument", "Stop on the pedestrian crossing", "Stop in the yellow box briefly"],
 "Junctions, crossings and yellow boxes are dangerous and usually illegal places to stop. Explain and pull in at the next safe spot."),
("Your engine warning light comes on mid-trip and the car loses power. What is the safest action?",
 "Pull over safely and get help", ["Finish the trip first, then check it", "Drive faster to reach the depot before it fails", "Ignore it while the car still moves"],
 "A fault that cuts power can leave you stranded in a dangerous place. Stop where it is safe, put the hazard lights on and arrange help and another vehicle for the passenger."),
("Which daily check helps keep your taxi or private hire car safe?",
 "Tyres, lights, brakes and wipers", ["Radio, mats and air freshener", "Meter tariff and receipt roll only", "Seat covers and phone charger"],
 "A quick check of tyres, lights, brakes, wipers and fluids before a shift catches faults before they cause a crash."),
("Your tyre tread looks very worn. Why should you change the tyre before your next shift?",
 "Grip falls sharply on wet roads", ["The car will fail its emissions test", "It makes the meter run faster", "Passengers will notice the noise"],
 "Worn tread cannot clear water, so the car can aquaplane and take much longer to stop in Singapore's heavy rain."),
("You are driving at night. When should you dip your headlights?",
 "When meeting oncoming traffic", ["Only when driving on the expressways", "Only when it is raining heavily", "When the street lights are switched off"],
 "High beam dazzles oncoming drivers and those you follow. Dip your lights whenever another road user could be blinded."),
("A passenger who has been drinking tries to grab the steering wheel. What should you do?",
 "Stop safely and ask them to stop", ["Speed up to reach the address", "Push their hand away while driving", "Keep driving and ignore it"],
 "Interference with the driver is dangerous. Pull over where it is safe, stay calm and call the police if the passenger will not stop."),
("A person on a personal mobility device is on the road beside your car. What should you expect?",
 "Sudden moves and low speed", ["Use of the expressway shoulder", "The same speed as a motorcycle", "Hand signals before every turn"],
 "Give vulnerable road users plenty of room. A small device rider is slow and can swerve without warning, so hold back and pass only with a wide gap."),
("You need to reverse out of a driveway at a condominium. What makes it safer?",
 "Reverse slowly, looking all round", ["Reverse quickly to clear the gate before cars come", "Rely only on the rear camera screen", "Ask the passenger to watch behind for you"],
 "Cameras and sensors help, but children and pedestrians can appear fast. Move slowly and keep looking all round, and get out to check if unsure."),
("Your car starts to aquaplane on a wet road. What should you do?",
 "Slow down with on/off braking", ["Brake hard and hold the pedal down", "Steer sharply towards the kerb", "Accelerate to push through the water"],
 "Aquaplaning takes away steering control and braking efficiency. Slow down by braking intermittently (on/off) until you regain control."),
("What gap does the Traffic Police handbook recommend behind the car ahead?",
 "At least three seconds", ["At least one second", "One car length at any speed", "Half a second on expressways"],
 "The Basic Theory of Driving uses the 'three-second' rule (previously two seconds): count three seconds from when the car ahead passes a fixed object."),
("You are tired and a passenger asks for a long trip to Tuas. What is the right choice?",
 "Decline it if you are unfit to drive", ["Accept it and drive with all the windows down", "Accept it and rest on the expressway shoulder", "Accept it but skip the vehicle checks"],
 "Refusing a hire without a reasonable excuse is an offence, but being unfit to drive safely is a real safety reason. Do not start a trip you cannot finish safely."),
("A motorcycle is filtering between lanes as traffic slows. What should you do?",
 "Check mirrors; avoid sudden moves", ["Close the gap in front to block it", "Move over quickly into the next lane to let it by", "Flash your headlights to warn it off"],
 "Motorcycles move through slow traffic. Hold your lane, signal early and check your mirrors before any move."),
("You feel angry after a rude driver cuts in front of you. What is the safest response?",
 "Let it go and keep a safe gap", ["Follow closely to show displeasure", "Overtake and brake in front", "Sound the horn for a long time"],
 "Retaliating turns a near miss into road rage. Let the other driver go and keep your attention on your passenger and the road."),
("Where is the safest place to set down a passenger on a busy road?",
 "A taxi stand, stop or driveway", ["The middle lane at a red light", "Beside a bus stop on the kerb", "In a yellow box junction"],
 "Designated taxi stands, taxi stops and building driveways are the safest places for passengers to get in and out."),
("Your passenger wants to get out while you wait in a traffic jam in the second lane. What should you do?",
 "Wait until you reach the kerb", ["Unlock the doors so they can walk across", "Tell them to use the right-hand door instead", "Let them out if no bus is near"],
 "Getting out in a live traffic lane puts the passenger between moving vehicles. Move to the kerb or a safe stopping place first."),
("A passenger in the back asks you to put their bag on the front passenger seat. What should you consider?",
 "It could fly forward if you brake hard", ["The bag might block the view of the meter", "It adds a luggage charge to the booking fee", "It delays printing the receipt"],
 "Loose items become missiles in a sudden stop. Put heavy items in the boot or secure them."),
]
